---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout title="Colophon | Sam Stringer-Hye" description="Tech stack and typography notes for this portfolio site." noindex>

  <section class="colophon-page" aria-label="Colophon">
    <h1 class="colophon-heading typo-display-md">Colophon</h1>
    <div class="colophon-row">
    <div class="colophon-body">

      <h2 class="typo-headline-lg">Tech Stack</h2>
      <p>
        Built with <strong>Astro</strong> for static-first delivery with vanilla TypeScript islands for interactive components.
        The hero runs on <strong>Three.js</strong>. Animations powered by <strong>GSAP</strong> (ScrollTrigger, SplitText).
        Smooth scrolling via <strong>Lenis</strong>. Deployed on <strong>Cloudflare Workers</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="typo-headline-lg">Typography</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Perfectly Nineties</strong> handles display and headline type, paired with
        <strong>DM Sans</strong> for body text, titles, labels, and UI elements.
        The serif carries the editorial voice; the sans keeps long text readable.
        The 5×3 typescale grid (display, headline, title, body, label × lg/md/sm) follows M3 conventions.
      </p>

      <h2 class="typo-headline-lg">Design Language</h2>
      <p>
        Every dot in the hero is drawn three times, in red, green and blue, each a beat behind the last, so each one reads as a pixel's three subpixels.
        The same three colors run through the scroll reveals, hover effects and carousel shadows.
        My first sketch was cyan, magenta and yellow ink. It ended up as light, which suits a site that opens with "Every pixel, on purpose."
      </p>

      <h2 class="typo-headline-lg">Credits</h2>
      <p>
        The devices on the work cards are 3D models from Sketchfab. The screens playing on them are the shipped work, as published in each case study.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/iphone-17-pro-4541aa8a28324b33a2baaf81d263aaec"><strong>iPhone 17 Pro</strong></a> and <a href="https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/macbook-neo-f3dd26684f114b1baffd1b0800876627"><strong>MacBook Neo</strong></a> by <a href="https://sketchfab.com/Ranguel">Ranguel</a>, licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>.<br />
        <a href="https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/apple-macbook-air-15-space-gray-2023-e8d82e341c794141a2561c2c9d01d79e"><strong>Apple Macbook Air 15 (Space Gray) 2023</strong></a> by <a href="https://sketchfab.com/akshatmittal">akshatmittal</a>, licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>.<br />
        <a href="https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/ipad-mini-6-2021-f363c2b1c74a462588db184bd4fb024e"><strong>iPad Mini 6 2021</strong></a> by <a href="https://sketchfab.com/DatSketch">DatSketch</a>, licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>.<br />
        <a href="https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/samsung-galaxy-s22-ultra-a95eec5181a24bcd8a8452df50b29f3a"><strong>Samsung Galaxy S22 Ultra</strong></a> and <a href="https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/galaxy-tab-s8-ultra-58228e3dc88743abb977d34717bb291e"><strong>Galaxy Tab S8 Ultra</strong></a> by <a href="https://sketchfab.com/DatSketch">DatSketch</a>, licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/">CC BY-NC 4.0</a>.<br />
        <a href="https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/samsung-galaxy-z-fold8-dfbcbd3143e644608c758edaa0289db3"><strong>SAMSUNG Galaxy Z Fold8</strong></a> by <a href="https://sketchfab.com/zhe_kan">zhe_kan</a>, licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. The adapted model this site serves is shared under the same license.
      </p>
      <p>
        Changes: each model is compressed, and the MacBook Neo, iPad and Fold are repainted in neutral gray. The phones and the Galaxy tablet are repainted in finishes they were sold in, with satin surfaces in place of the files’ textured ones. The Fold file keeps only the unfolded phone, and the Galaxy phone and tablet leave out the S Pens modeled beside them.
      </p>
      <p>
        The iPhone home screens on the Whataburger card come from the iOS 27 kit in <a href="https://developer.apple.com/design/resources/">Apple Design Resources</a>, with the Whataburger icon in place of a sample app.
      </p>
      <p>
        The icons around the photo on the About page are built in code with three.js, after the visionOS app icon style. Where WebGL isn't available, flat icons from <a href="https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-emoji"><strong>Fluent Emoji</strong></a> by Microsoft (<a href="https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-emoji/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT License</a>) stand in.
      </p>

      <h2 class="typo-headline-lg">Accessibility</h2>
      <p>
        This site respects <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>: all animations are disabled or minimized when the user has requested reduced motion.
        Navigation is fully keyboard-accessible with focus trapping on mobile, and all images include alt text.
      </p>

      <p style="margin-top: var(--space-5);">
        <a href="/#work" class="colophon-work-link typo-ui-caps">View work →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .colophon-work-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: var(--touch-target);
  }

  .colophon-page {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: subgrid;
  }

  .colophon-heading {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin: 0;
    padding-block: var(--space-6);
    padding-inline: var(--content-inset-md);
  }

  .colophon-row {
    position: relative;
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: subgrid;
  }

  .colophon-row::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: var(--border-width-1);
    background: var(--color-rule);
    transform: scaleX(var(--border-draw, 1));
    transform-origin: left;
  }


  .colophon-body {
    grid-column: 4 / 10;
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
  }

  @media (--2x) {
    .colophon-heading {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      padding-inline: var(--content-inset-sm);
    }

    .colophon-body {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      padding-inline: var(--content-inset-sm);
    }
  }

  .colophon-body h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .colophon-body h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .colophon-body p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    max-width: var(--prose-measure);
  }

  .colophon-body strong {
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  .colophon-body code {
    background: var(--prose-code-bg);
    padding: var(--prose-code-padding-block) var(--prose-code-padding-inline);
    border-radius: var(--prose-code-border-radius);
  }
</style>
